# English-only docs and code comments

## Docs (committed)

- Tracked Markdown is **English only**: `README.md`, `docs/**` (except ignored paths), `tui/README.md`, `.cursor/skills/**/*.md`, `.github/**/*.md`.
- Do **not** commit Russian (or other non-English) product/spec docs.

## Code comments

- Comments and docstrings in committed source must be **English only**.
- Applies to: `*.ts`, `*.tsx`, `*.js`, `*.mjs`, `*.rs`, `*.sql`, shell scripts, Dockerfiles, etc.
- Prefer short why-comments; do not leave Russian TODOs, section headers, or inline notes in tracked code.

## Local Russian / scratch

- Informal or Russian working notes are allowed **only** under `docs/dev/` (gitignored).
- Never `git add` `docs/dev/` or other ignored scratch paths.
- Lasting design notes → English under tracked `docs/`.

## Agent behavior

- Editing tracked docs or adding comments → English.
- User asks for Russian notes for themselves → `docs/dev/`, do not stage.
- Do not mix languages in the same committed doc or comment block.
